From: Simeon Marijon <simeon.marijon@st.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Feb 2025 17:23:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 535/913] mod/scmi_voltage_domain: validate element_id

Previously the function called test but return no error

outligned by coverity

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 9053beb82aff06622b359938686a60f22ec3da2a mod/scmi_voltage_domain: validate element_id]
Change-Id: I0fb642693da538e57c5606732583a9295c0f524b
Signed-off-by: Simeon Marijon <simeon.marijon@st.com>
---
 .../module/scmi_voltage_domain/src/mod_scmi_voltage_domain.c   | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_voltage_domain/src/mod_scmi_voltage_domain.c b/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_voltage_domain/src/mod_scmi_voltage_domain.c
index 60c723fd5..ab6b7ebf8 100644
--- a/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_voltage_domain/src/mod_scmi_voltage_domain.c
+++ b/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_voltage_domain/src/mod_scmi_voltage_domain.c
@@ -159,7 +159,8 @@ static int get_device(fwk_id_t service_id, unsigned int elt_idx,
         return FWK_E_RANGE;
 
     device = &agent->device_table[elt_idx];
-    fwk_module_is_valid_element_id(device->element_id);
+
+    fwk_assert(fwk_module_is_valid_element_id(device->element_id));
 
     if (out_device)
         *out_device = device;
